hexagonrpcd 0.4.0 for sunstone's sensors PD (applied by add-hexagonrpcd.sh)

SM4375's SSC (the sensors PD on the ADSP) rewrites its registry at every start: it reads
persist/sensors/registry/sns_reg_version and registry/, then for each JSON in
/vendor/etc/sensors/config writes ../temp.json and renames it into registry/. Upstream
hexagonrpcd serves files read-only, so the first write fails, the registry task asserts
(sns_registry_sensor.c:154) and the whole ADSP restarts (audio too). This adds:

- -W DIR: persist/sensors/registry is DIR, writable (a private copy of the registry, never the
  persist partition). Only mapped_rw directories can be written; writes stay inside them (single
  path segments, ".." handled above the physical directories, new files never through symlinks).
- apps_std fopen modes w/a/+, fwrite (5), fremove (24) and frename (33).
- Methods from 31 on: the method field has 5 bits, so they come as 31 with the real number in the
  first input number (stat, 31, already had it as its unused first number).
- Input buffers larger than the 256 bytes next2 returns are fetched with get_in_bufs2 (up to 1 MiB).
- A call that cannot be made (unknown handle or method, bad buffers) fails alone instead of ending
  the daemon: the PD asks for a local "sns_registry" interface that does not exist here.

